; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; Auto-generated by AutoAnsys — Fluent SOLVER from existing mesh.cas.h5
; ANSYS 2025R1 — assumes the mesh artifact has already been written by a
; previous mesh-only job (mesh_only.jou.j2).
;
; Faithfully mirrors the CFD specialist's working ARC command-window flow:
;   /report/reference-values/...  →  /define/models/viscous/...  →
;   /define/boundary-conditions/...  →  /solve/init/hyb-init  →
;   /solve/iterate <N>  →  /file/write-case-data
; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

; ── Load the pre-built case ──────────────────────────────────────────
/file/read-case "/scratch/<user>/autoansys/jobs/<job_id>/mesh.cas.h5"

; ── Print zone list for debugging ────────────────────────────────────
; Scheme, not %py-exec: this journal runs in a pure solver launch (no -meshing)
; where the meshing Python API is not available.
(display "=== ZONE LIST ===")(newline)
/define/boundary-conditions/list-zones

; NOTE: no `zone-type enclosure fluid` safety net here. Both mesh workflows
; deliver a correct fluid cell zone in mesh.cas.h5 (VWT: `tunnel-fluid`), and on
; meshes without an `enclosure` zone the line aborts the journal even when
; wrapped in ti-menu-load-string (probe 6380500: "Invalid zone" then a scheme
; CAR error from the leftover args). The legacy combined template keeps it —
; the SOP path guarantees that zone exists there.

; ── Reference values, turbulence model, all BCs (shared partial) ─────
; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; SHARED BC + REFERENCE-VALUES BLOCK
; Included by both solver_from_case.jou.j2 (split workflow) and
; mesh_watertight.jou.j2 Phase 2 (combined workflow).
;
; Each BC list emits one Fluent TUI command per entry. The argument order
; mirrors the working specialist script (Max Squat full-car) byte-for-byte
; so reproducing it as a flat journal yields the same setup as the manual
; /define/boundary-conditions/... typing in the ARC command window.
; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

; ── Reference Values ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
; density is required for physical force COEFFICIENTS (AUDIT C4 — was unset).
/report/reference-values/area 1.2
/report/reference-values/length 2.8
/report/reference-values/velocity 15.65
/report/reference-values/density 1.225

; ── Turbulence Model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
/define/models/viscous/kw-sst? yes
/define/models/viscous/curvature-correction? yes


; ── Velocity inlets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
/define/boundary-conditions/velocity-inlet inlet no no yes yes no 15.65 no 0. no no yes 5.0 10.0

; ── Rotating walls (wheels) ──────────────────────────────────────────
; TUI: zone yes motion-bc-moving no no yes yes no no 0. no 0.5 no <ω> <ox> <oy> <oz> <ax> <ay> <az>

; ── Translating walls (e.g. moving ground) ───────────────────────────
; TUI: zone yes motion-bc-moving no no yes no no <vel> <dx> <dy> <dz> no no 0. no 0.5

; ── Slip / specified-shear walls (tunnel walls, contact patches) ─────
; TUI: zone no yes shear-bc-spec-shear no no 0. no 0.5 no 0. no 0. no 0.
/define/boundary-conditions/zone-type farfield-top wall
/define/boundary-conditions/wall farfield-top no yes shear-bc-spec-shear no no 0. no 0.5 no 0. no 0. no 0.
/define/boundary-conditions/zone-type farfield-side wall
/define/boundary-conditions/wall farfield-side no yes shear-bc-spec-shear no no 0. no 0.5 no 0. no 0. no 0.

; ── Stationary no-slip walls ─────────────────────────────────────────
; Default Fluent wall behaviour; we just pin the zone-type explicitly.
/define/boundary-conditions/zone-type ground wall
/define/boundary-conditions/zone-type body wall

; ── Pressure outlets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
; 2025R1: the parameter is `gauge-pressure` — `pgauge` is rejected as an
; invalid command (verified on ARC, probe 6380260).
/define/boundary-conditions/zone-type outlet pressure-outlet
/define/boundary-conditions/set/pressure-outlet outlet () gauge-pressure no 0.0 quit

; ── Symmetry planes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
/define/boundary-conditions/zone-type symmetry symmetry

; ── Solution Methods (2025R1-validated TUI, probes 6380286–6380410) ────
; The TUI takes NUMERIC enums, not names ("Coupled"/"second-order" raise
; "unbound variable"/"Invalid integer" and abort the journal). Config keeps the
; human-readable names; this partial maps them.
/solve/set/p-v-coupling 24
; gradient-scheme: left at the case default (least-squares cell based) — the
; TUI form is a yes/no prompt pair; [needs-cluster] wire if a non-default is needed.
/solve/set/discretization-scheme/pressure 12
/solve/set/discretization-scheme/mom 1
/solve/set/discretization-scheme/k 1
/solve/set/discretization-scheme/omega 1

; ── Report definitions, report files, convergence (shared partial) ───
; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; SHARED REPORTS + CONVERGENCE BLOCK
; Included by solver_from_case.jou.j2 and mesh_watertight.jou.j2 so the two
; never diverge (a past divergence left the combined journal with undefined
; contour-surface variables — AUDIT C7).
;
; Forces/moment are integrated over the BODY wall zone(s) only, via
; reporting.body_wall_pattern — NOT the previous `thread-names *`, which also
; summed the moving ground and tunnel walls (AUDIT C3). Outputs are FORCES in
; Newtons (drag_force, lift_force, mom_y). The coefficients Cd/Cl/Cm and the
; half-model symmetry doubling are computed downstream in app/post/forces.py
; from these forces + the reference values, so the journal does not depend on
; the version-specific coefficient-report TUI.
; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


; ── Report Definitions (body-scoped forces; AUDIT C2/C3) ──────────────
; 2025R1-validated (probes 6380332/6380354): force defs take force-vector +
; thread-names; the MOMENT def takes `mom-center` + `mom-axis` (the older
; `moment-vector`/`moment-center` pair is rejected).
/solve/report-definitions/add drag_force force force-vector 1 0 0 thread-names body () quit
/solve/report-definitions/add lift_force force force-vector 0 0 1 thread-names body () quit
/solve/report-definitions/add mom_y moment mom-center 0.0 0.0 0.0 mom-axis 0 1 0 thread-names body () quit

; ── Report Files ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Residuals: `report-files/add ... report-type iteration` is NOT valid 2025R1
; TUI (probe 6380354) — residual history is parsed from the transcript
; (fluent.log) instead; the tolerant parser (app/post/report_files.py) handles it.
/solve/report-files/add forces-report report-defs drag_force lift_force mom_y () file-name "/scratch/<user>/autoansys/jobs/<individual_part_job>/forces.csv" print? yes quit

; ── Convergence Monitors ──────────────────────────────────────────────
/solve/monitors/residual/convergence-criteria 0.0001 0.0001 0.0001 0.0001 0.0001 0.0001
; Force-plateau convergence (AUDIT C5): the guessed
; `/solve/convergence-conditions/add ...` phrase is NOT valid 2025R1 TUI
; (probe 6380382: invalid command "add"). Until the correct syntax is
; discovered (help-dump probe pending), the fixed `/solve/iterate N` below is
; the stop condition — convergence is then judged from the forces.csv plateau
; in post-processing. config: convergence.use_force_convergence reserved.

; ── Initialize ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/solve/init/hyb-init

; ── Save case before iterating ───────────────────────────────────────
; DISTINCT name from the post-solve write: writing case-data over an existing
; file triggers an overwrite-confirm prompt in batch that eats the next journal
; line — result.dat.h5 silently never got written (probe 6387661).
/file/write-case "/scratch/<user>/autoansys/jobs/<individual_part_job>/setup.cas.h5"

; ── Iterate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/solve/iterate 300

; ── Export Results ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
/file/write-case-data "/scratch/<user>/autoansys/jobs/<individual_part_job>/result.cas.h5"

; ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; PHASE 4: POST-PROCESSING — Contour Images (shared partial)
; ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; SHARED CONTOUR / POST-PROCESSING BLOCK — 2025R1-validated (probe 6388066;
; views validated probes 6388814/6389014, imagery confirmed job 6388594).
;
; Idiom notes (all verified live on ARC):
; • Requires the solver stage to launch with `-gu -driver null` — with `-g`
;   the graphics subsystem is absent and `display save-picture` does not exist.
; • Every command goes through (ti-menu-load-string "...") — TUI menu state
;   persists across journal lines and leading `/` resolves RELATIVE to the
;   current menu, so bare paths desync after any menu-entering command.
; • Contours are display OBJECTS (`display objects create contour ...`) — the
;   legacy /display/set/contours/* menu no longer exists.
; • View commands only affect an EXISTING graphics window, and the headless
;   window is created lazily by the first `display` — so the order per image
;   must be: display (bootstrap) → camera → display again (redraw) →
;   auto-scale (fit content, keeps direction) → save-picture. A views command
;   issued before any display, or a save without re-display, yields an empty
;   canvas (probes 6388814/6389014).
; ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


(ti-menu-load-string "display set picture driver png")
(ti-menu-load-string "display set picture x-resolution 1920")
(ti-menu-load-string "display set picture y-resolution 1080")

; Mid-SPAN cross-section for flow-field views (validated arg order). In the
; team's CAD convention z is UP (ground at z=0, probe 6380144 extents) — the
; side-view slice is y=0 (imagery confirmed on job 6388594).
(ti-menu-load-string "surface iso-surface y-coordinate midplane-y () () 0 ()")

; DEFAULT VIEW ONLY. The camera/restore-view sequence renders EMPTY canvases
; on real solved cases even with re-display + auto-scale (fc29p-fc31p, jobs
; 6408623/6408669/6408714 — views apply per the axis triad but no content
; draws under -driver null). The default view is the only rendering path
; proven to produce content (acceptance-2 job 6388594 + fc31p). Sideways
; framing remains an open polish item — do NOT reintroduce view commands
; without a probe-validated recipe. Also: save-picture on an EXISTING file
; raises an overwrite prompt that desyncs the journal (fc30p) — filenames
; here are safe only because production workspaces are unique per job.
(ti-menu-load-string "display objects create contour cont-velocity field velocity-magnitude surfaces-list midplane-y () quit")
(ti-menu-load-string "display objects display cont-velocity")
(ti-menu-load-string "display save-picture \"/scratch/<user>/autoansys/jobs/<individual_part_job>/contour_velocity_midplane.png\"")

(ti-menu-load-string "display objects create contour cont-pressure field pressure surfaces-list midplane-y () quit")
(ti-menu-load-string "display objects display cont-pressure")
(ti-menu-load-string "display save-picture \"/scratch/<user>/autoansys/jobs/<individual_part_job>/contour_pressure_midplane.png\"")

(ti-menu-load-string "display objects create contour cont-tke field turb-kinetic-energy surfaces-list midplane-y () quit")
(ti-menu-load-string "display objects display cont-tke")
(ti-menu-load-string "display save-picture \"/scratch/<user>/autoansys/jobs/<individual_part_job>/contour_tke_midplane.png\"")

; Pressure coefficient on the body walls.
(ti-menu-load-string "display objects create contour cont-cp field pressure-coefficient surfaces-list body () quit")
(ti-menu-load-string "display objects display cont-cp")
(ti-menu-load-string "display save-picture \"/scratch/<user>/autoansys/jobs/<individual_part_job>/contour_cp.png\"")

/exit yes
